{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:12e88a8cc2e681c53234ab6a048049585088143cab8f7f5b2a631956778ed071","title":"How can an internal volume become very large while one four-cycle remains comparatively small? This example separates the growing cycle \\(\\tau_5\\) from the smaller cycle \\(\\tau_4\\) through a difference of their three-halves powers.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:120c2cb0b711c90fe2146fad6110c576a6d9f5bb61a2282eb9193a32adbc0781","title":"The scalar excursion depends on how the dark component shares the expansion rate with independently specified matter. Distinguishing baryon-only matter from a separate dark-matter component is essential when a Chaplygin fluid may itself unify dark matter and dark energy.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12db93fcd7db364da2e8233a53f7284428d51bf5123cea9ed11088568c2244bc","title":"How can two supergravity sectors be coupled so that F-term uplifting preserves moduli supersymmetric critical points and shift symmetries, while retaining stability under Minkowski or de Sitter uplift?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12b3fcd813834073f60cbc502ab5faad5196684000cc645c3ca972e79919f856","title":"How can interacting quantum fields generate dissipation, radiation and stochastic inflaton fluctuations during inflation, and under what conditions do these effects support viable warm inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12e160fd80767cc324b039cc9336561b9886db0bcef8564120b6038aaefe35fe","title":"How do geometric Type-IIA O6 flux compactifications map precisely to N = 4 gauging parameters and consistency constraints, and which previously known N = 1 AdS₄ vacua admit extended-supergravity embeddings?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1267ad152999e8bed740db67d205719eb4fd3bed3613d64765a5e0709d708ad8","title":"Can small periodic corrections to a linear axion-monodromy inflationary potential produce observable primordial non-Gaussianity while leaving little detectable structure in the scalar power spectrum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:126be64c9635a96625961af1030369808590194a10075103d8acbba3e473e864","title":"How far do anomaly cancellation and physical gauge kinetic terms constrain discrete 6D supergravity data, and can their relation to F-theory geometry establish or obstruct string universality?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0009"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12d6b2840c30966c0c255f5200bd76479e4e85e483e32d8f291d417bca0260fc","title":"How can CFT operators represent interacting bulk observables beyond leading large N while satisfying bulk locality, defined as commutation at spacelike separation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:125ac7f0a914cf1c69b47b22372b102f78a6e8de8defd11d210e64935897c217","title":"Can the Giddings–Strominger semi-wormhole be interpreted as an on-shell torsional instanton carrying Nieh–Yan charge, and can tunneling between those charge sectors realize a topological quantum vacuum associated with the Barbero–Immirzi parameter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1207056f985a2f152dfe58b2fc4b8148b8d3ef843a2793972033fc78cb928552","title":"Can hidden-sector F-term uplifting induced by D-term stabilization be understood by expanding a higher-dimensional D7 theory around a supersymmetric T-brane background, and can the resulting contribution support de Sitter LVS minima?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:128c33b062efbd5f7d0ab2dac047acfaf0e181cc4a735bdf0722e85f802b5965","title":"Determine the propagating spectra of four-dimensional N=1,2,3,4 Weyl supergravities by taking the massless limit of Einstein–Weyl theories and accounting for enhanced gauge symmetries; investigate higher conformal tensors and possible holographic interpretations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12cdd8fbd68ae294e0c474b9ab27c43c725b1aba10c3233fd91e921ec92bf268","title":"What are the leading finite-temperature vacuum-decay rates for charged spin-0 and spin-1/2 particles in simultaneous homogeneous electric and magnetic fields, and how do magnetic fields and spin modify the worldline-instanton result?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12671ccc373672d6f903c29382ed77e24134d93ce6f55653391464fa403948dd","title":"Which microscopic interaction regimes can supply dissipation strong enough to affect inflation without invalidating the potential through thermal corrections? The three laws represent different mediator hierarchies and protection mechanisms.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:12eae58b9077aee00ffe4e1ecac22023960e29dd3643d78b90fc229e5edb7afd","title":"These compactifications allow period geometry to determine scalar distances and BPS central charges, providing explicit geometric tests of the distance conjecture.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"i